			"type": "Line",
			"value": " A `new` callee's `.prop` lookups never break — prettier's `printMemberExpression`",
			"start": 10,
			"end": 94
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " inlines every lookup whose chain IS the callee (member.js",
			"start": 96,
			"end": 156
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " `shouldInlineNewExpressionCallee`), so the constructor name prints as one unbreakable",
			"start": 158,
			"end": 246
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " unit and the width falls to the argument list, or overflows.",
			"start": 248,
			"end": 311
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " 100 — fits inline",
			"start": 314,
			"end": 334
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " 101 — the callee has no break point, so it stays intact and overflows",
